[[:db/retract 17592186134308 :question/answer-fields 17592186131887] {:db/id 17592186133833 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-caddd05b-4c41-5309-addf-23d1dae6b262" "question-c0966490-d3a0-58c5-8173-708ac9df5606"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133834 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-65ffb8b6-5f3a-587e-8cef-ea786c6bad11" "question-44763ea7-5c70-59d7-96b0-261e9cae9fe6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133835 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5a3b41b5-2d15-5da0-8405-0eae05fe096e" "question-7dc3d2ae-4ebe-55e5-a13e-304e391443f7" "question-fd9da944-934f-55d2-b2c0-f2a5f1dc8cbe"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134308 :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/da/da2895c09bc33f628626257b6d102e74875825df14ba744904e02ffa71552a02.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,2{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1+{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-caddd05b-4c41-5309-addf-23d1dae6b262" :question/id #uuid "caddd05b-4c41-5309-addf-23d1dae6b262" :question/math-academy-id "q-132116" :question/problem "![](images/e7/e72e6dea415bf05a89518d14dcf932d22cc5774919250638716274d71563c621.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y=\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{2}$ and $y=\\sqrt{x},$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/1a/1ab9ae94853a0d161c74aa8d79c47a38f0b0453e0ece320c367098794d5bcb59.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{2}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/8}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/8}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-79781c7a-5527-5df8-af52-34fca02e52a3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-79781c7a-5527-5df8-af52-34fca02e52a3" :answer-field/id #uuid "79781c7a-5527-5df8-af52-34fca02e52a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8446a67f-16fd-5996-8bfe-116829320e65" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9652bca8-4c39-5835-8b2f-41295a63651e" "answer-8446a67f-16fd-5996-8bfe-116829320e65" "answer-0d894768-8a15-5793-b9bc-b08a5588612c" "answer-2aecbf82-cfb7-5a1b-9476-c47c24aef735" "answer-0e26bbbc-a0dd-5dcf-a436-06546654bda6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9652bca8-4c39-5835-8b2f-41295a63651e" :answer/id #uuid "9652bca8-4c39-5835-8b2f-41295a63651e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{{x}^{2}/8}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8446a67f-16fd-5996-8bfe-116829320e65" :answer/id #uuid "8446a67f-16fd-5996-8bfe-116829320e65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/8}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d894768-8a15-5793-b9bc-b08a5588612c" :answer/id #uuid "0d894768-8a15-5793-b9bc-b08a5588612c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/8}^{4}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2aecbf82-cfb7-5a1b-9476-c47c24aef735" :answer/id #uuid "2aecbf82-cfb7-5a1b-9476-c47c24aef735" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/8}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e26bbbc-a0dd-5dcf-a436-06546654bda6" :answer/id #uuid "0e26bbbc-a0dd-5dcf-a436-06546654bda6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/8}^{\\sqrt{x}}[{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134517 :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/4f/4fec059132b7bd02cb64f864b6982c0c64a66c22646334ca199fad12097ba435.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 2{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-c0966490-d3a0-58c5-8173-708ac9df5606" :question/id #uuid "c0966490-d3a0-58c5-8173-708ac9df5606" :question/math-academy-id "q-81322" :question/problem "![](images/16/16ec458c15c9427d3d57c6628438b6aa93960778a46c5df162de5d79b87704c9.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y={x}^{3}$ and $y=\\sqrt{x},$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/8f/8f18afd79cafdcd0696b3bc25c05fec4109e54cccb084eef49544a4d6599526c.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-891e04a1-4341-5ccc-83ec-77966d206b4b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-891e04a1-4341-5ccc-83ec-77966d206b4b" :answer-field/id #uuid "891e04a1-4341-5ccc-83ec-77966d206b4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0e76eacb-ab50-512f-8bc9-2e40397aa3c4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ce0b8e5e-97b6-5103-a165-688538eefcc0" "answer-d10e9547-3b6b-5eff-be0f-bc44381d318d" "answer-0e76eacb-ab50-512f-8bc9-2e40397aa3c4" "answer-515b98b5-a932-5692-ab25-5bf641f668aa" "answer-e159d3af-176c-5a17-ac50-a511cbc5021c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce0b8e5e-97b6-5103-a165-688538eefcc0" :answer/id #uuid "ce0b8e5e-97b6-5103-a165-688538eefcc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d10e9547-3b6b-5eff-be0f-bc44381d318d" :answer/id #uuid "d10e9547-3b6b-5eff-be0f-bc44381d318d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{{x}^{3}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e76eacb-ab50-512f-8bc9-2e40397aa3c4" :answer/id #uuid "0e76eacb-ab50-512f-8bc9-2e40397aa3c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-515b98b5-a932-5692-ab25-5bf641f668aa" :answer/id #uuid "515b98b5-a932-5692-ab25-5bf641f668aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{{x}^{3}}[{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e159d3af-176c-5a17-ac50-a511cbc5021c" :answer/id #uuid "e159d3af-176c-5a17-ac50-a511cbc5021c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{\\sqrt{x}}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351291 :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/5d/5d56dfdb75870a251f1eb94f0305a083489ce9e8dc4b9843138cd8ef88da30ab.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,2{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 4x+6\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{4x+6}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186326875 :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =4 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$0\\le x\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/54/54f366679684823341bab818459ce5fc884ebbdd2376e800b781d1b832c4ba64.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,2x\\le y\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{4}{y}^{2}\\sqrt{x}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-65ffb8b6-5f3a-587e-8cef-ea786c6bad11" :question/id #uuid "65ffb8b6-5f3a-587e-8cef-ea786c6bad11" :question/math-academy-id "q-132217" :question/problem "![](images/45/45675650564d0e0afa5a1cf1a3f4c786c3443374dee2662e9eb44c10f94089c3.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y={x}^{3}$ and $y=4x$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}(x+{y}^{2})\\,dA=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & ={x}^{3} \\\\ {x}^{3}-4x & =0 \\\\ x(x-2)(x+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe discard $x=-2$ since $x\\ge 0$ in our region. Therefore, $x$-limits are $0\\le x\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/a7/a7bda76c722de10b988f108c79334227ba2cda82535764ffef76450edaccbb07.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le 4x\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(x+{y}^{2})\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{4x}(x+{y}^{2})\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ea44a1a7-ed98-5bc5-89ba-bb9dd69cb232"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ea44a1a7-ed98-5bc5-89ba-bb9dd69cb232" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea44a1a7-ed98-5bc5-89ba-bb9dd69cb232" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d2128234-83d0-5812-ae71-d08ebe9f38a6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3da44e10-730a-5257-a521-a8770302d81d" "answer-d2128234-83d0-5812-ae71-d08ebe9f38a6" "answer-4e3a7c89-e6ea-552b-afe0-e00f4ee15120" "answer-591afc4d-4698-5d08-922d-35f248a7e719" "answer-905505a9-14b5-5198-8f09-6a3975f0713b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3da44e10-730a-5257-a521-a8770302d81d" :answer/id #uuid "3da44e10-730a-5257-a521-a8770302d81d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{4x}^{{x}^{3}}(x+{y}^{2})\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2128234-83d0-5812-ae71-d08ebe9f38a6" :answer/id #uuid "d2128234-83d0-5812-ae71-d08ebe9f38a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{4x}(x+{y}^{2})\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e3a7c89-e6ea-552b-afe0-e00f4ee15120" :answer/id #uuid "4e3a7c89-e6ea-552b-afe0-e00f4ee15120" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4x}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{2}(x+{y}^{2})\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-591afc4d-4698-5d08-922d-35f248a7e719" :answer/id #uuid "591afc4d-4698-5d08-922d-35f248a7e719" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4x}(x+{y}^{2})\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-905505a9-14b5-5198-8f09-6a3975f0713b" :answer/id #uuid "905505a9-14b5-5198-8f09-6a3975f0713b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{4x}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(x+{y}^{2})\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186326882 :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{x}^{2} & =9-{x}^{2} \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$-2\\le x\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/c5/c56c5be4ac88755f1859f295f700be8710d75b16380ac120e6b56a3aa767acbe.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,1+{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 9-{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{9-{x}^{2}}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186326883 :question/worked-solution "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](images/fc/fcb347767983c38eb12f521ca556dcc5a96705ee4e887fb8d43c42984dfe1a26.png)\n\nNow, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x} & =\\sqrt{x} \\\\ x\\sqrt{x} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\sqrt{x})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =1 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$1\\le x\\le 4.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/91/91bf7087e5aa0053d24cb45158d48b0bb36fb84b28ebabaeba3c26dc62168dfe.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\frac{1}{x}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{1/x}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-44763ea7-5c70-59d7-96b0-261e9cae9fe6" :question/id #uuid "44763ea7-5c70-59d7-96b0-261e9cae9fe6" :question/math-academy-id "q-132244" :question/problem "If $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y=\\frac{1}{2}x$ and $y=\\sqrt{x},$ then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](images/51/51d1e26c53fd0b3ae404df652eed41cd19604d0358ecb5f4e09727580fc57304.png)\n\nNow, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x & =\\sqrt{x} \\\\ x & =2\\sqrt{x} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =(2\\sqrt{x})^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4x \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x & =0 \\\\ x(x-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$0\\le x\\le 4.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/05/05740cccba899218f50fc2d9867b968c2b32ca7eaf3ab22a3519387d5756b394.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\frac{1}{2}x\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{x/2}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{x/2}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9a452cbd-b41e-57a2-b9c8-171ce59710e6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9a452cbd-b41e-57a2-b9c8-171ce59710e6" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a452cbd-b41e-57a2-b9c8-171ce59710e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c5c07fef-6aeb-50a3-89df-5c39d2dd7e42" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0e8c72e1-95ce-588f-83ca-66cb68683c6c" "answer-c5c07fef-6aeb-50a3-89df-5c39d2dd7e42" "answer-143a6761-d36c-525c-8e83-45c2a57cbbb3" "answer-db0ed10f-43bd-5529-89ae-a406abfd9be5" "answer-fccd0839-e8ff-574c-b365-2b3560292e70"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e8c72e1-95ce-588f-83ca-66cb68683c6c" :answer/id #uuid "0e8c72e1-95ce-588f-83ca-66cb68683c6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{x/2}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5c07fef-6aeb-50a3-89df-5c39d2dd7e42" :answer/id #uuid "c5c07fef-6aeb-50a3-89df-5c39d2dd7e42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{x/2}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-143a6761-d36c-525c-8e83-45c2a57cbbb3" :answer/id #uuid "143a6761-d36c-525c-8e83-45c2a57cbbb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}[{\\int }_{x/2}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db0ed10f-43bd-5529-89ae-a406abfd9be5" :answer/id #uuid "db0ed10f-43bd-5529-89ae-a406abfd9be5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{x/2}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fccd0839-e8ff-574c-b365-2b3560292e70" :answer/id #uuid "fccd0839-e8ff-574c-b365-2b3560292e70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{x/2}^{\\sqrt{x}}[{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5a3b41b5-2d15-5da0-8405-0eae05fe096e" :question/id #uuid "5a3b41b5-2d15-5da0-8405-0eae05fe096e" :question/math-academy-id "q-132278" :question/problem "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+2}4x\\,dy\\,dx=$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+2}4x\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4x[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+2}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4x[\\,y\\,]_{{x}^{2}}^{x+2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4x(x+2-{x}^{2})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(4{x}^{2}+8x-4{x}^{3})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(4{x}^{2}+8x-4{x}^{3})\\,dx & ={[\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{32}{3}+16-16)-(\\frac{4}{3}+4-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}-\\frac{13}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-88db635a-9530-5e97-bdb9-19d4d9fad8ff"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-88db635a-9530-5e97-bdb9-19d4d9fad8ff" :answer-field/id #uuid "88db635a-9530-5e97-bdb9-19d4d9fad8ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a4b2488a-48f0-57ea-8da8-293b1968eff9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7c0ff31b-b685-5181-bcf5-fcb4b5fb5898" "answer-fba47bb6-4852-5809-a223-aeaa8a4552b9" "answer-a4b2488a-48f0-57ea-8da8-293b1968eff9" "answer-cd3c9235-9213-5c04-8371-0593ba1e7d3b" "answer-c9e03770-ad7c-5b2c-8772-04bb85575952"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c0ff31b-b685-5181-bcf5-fcb4b5fb5898" :answer/id #uuid "7c0ff31b-b685-5181-bcf5-fcb4b5fb5898" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fba47bb6-4852-5809-a223-aeaa8a4552b9" :answer/id #uuid "fba47bb6-4852-5809-a223-aeaa8a4552b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4b2488a-48f0-57ea-8da8-293b1968eff9" :answer/id #uuid "a4b2488a-48f0-57ea-8da8-293b1968eff9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd3c9235-9213-5c04-8371-0593ba1e7d3b" :answer/id #uuid "cd3c9235-9213-5c04-8371-0593ba1e7d3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9e03770-ad7c-5b2c-8772-04bb85575952" :answer/id #uuid "c9e03770-ad7c-5b2c-8772-04bb85575952" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7dc3d2ae-4ebe-55e5-a13e-304e391443f7" :question/id #uuid "7dc3d2ae-4ebe-55e5-a13e-304e391443f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-81347" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,dy\\,dx=$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡y}{2}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡0}{2})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b7552f1e-9180-5b58-ac47-de556c1b13e3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b7552f1e-9180-5b58-ac47-de556c1b13e3" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7552f1e-9180-5b58-ac47-de556c1b13e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f647841e-742e-5179-a5c3-3b9852200fd3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c56a9809-f9cb-5e51-a1c8-7aa478b44cda" "answer-c1fc5106-7c16-50e1-afac-b55e9efdb392" "answer-f647841e-742e-5179-a5c3-3b9852200fd3" "answer-042a3167-88c1-58d7-9cb9-db2e59913bc6" "answer-0bcb67a6-a89e-5cb5-bf50-d01668c64856"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c56a9809-f9cb-5e51-a1c8-7aa478b44cda" :answer/id #uuid "c56a9809-f9cb-5e51-a1c8-7aa478b44cda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1fc5106-7c16-50e1-afac-b55e9efdb392" :answer/id #uuid "c1fc5106-7c16-50e1-afac-b55e9efdb392" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f647841e-742e-5179-a5c3-3b9852200fd3" :answer/id #uuid "f647841e-742e-5179-a5c3-3b9852200fd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-042a3167-88c1-58d7-9cb9-db2e59913bc6" :answer/id #uuid "042a3167-88c1-58d7-9cb9-db2e59913bc6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡1-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0bcb67a6-a89e-5cb5-bf50-d01668c64856" :answer/id #uuid "0bcb67a6-a89e-5cb5-bf50-d01668c64856" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡1-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fd9da944-934f-55d2-b2c0-f2a5f1dc8cbe" :question/id #uuid "fd9da944-934f-55d2-b2c0-f2a5f1dc8cbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-81349" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2-x}2y\\,dy\\,dx.$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2-x}2y\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2-x}2y\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{y}^{2}]_{{x}^{2}}^{2-x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}((2-x)^{2}-{x}^{4})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-{x}^{4}+{x}^{2}-4x+4)\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-{x}^{4}+{x}^{2}-4x+4)\\,dx & =-{[\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-2{x}^{2}+4x]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{3}-2+4-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-31d1310b-4a61-5d68-8a57-0e17be92a021"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-31d1310b-4a61-5d68-8a57-0e17be92a021" :answer-field/id #uuid "31d1310b-4a61-5d68-8a57-0e17be92a021" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7ee10c12-4af0-5db5-b53d-68778b815ab0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-678a88ce-8652-55f7-93ad-13e8a6e7dc60" "answer-280f2ce9-93ce-54c2-8464-00d7c0d0608f" "answer-a9114ff3-e2ba-5ae9-832c-adc5cedc81f6" "answer-7ee10c12-4af0-5db5-b53d-68778b815ab0" "answer-96aa0f31-717f-5964-8ba0-b359e5264a03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-678a88ce-8652-55f7-93ad-13e8a6e7dc60" :answer/id #uuid "678a88ce-8652-55f7-93ad-13e8a6e7dc60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-280f2ce9-93ce-54c2-8464-00d7c0d0608f" :answer/id #uuid "280f2ce9-93ce-54c2-8464-00d7c0d0608f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{32}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9114ff3-e2ba-5ae9-832c-adc5cedc81f6" :answer/id #uuid "a9114ff3-e2ba-5ae9-832c-adc5cedc81f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ee10c12-4af0-5db5-b53d-68778b815ab0" :answer/id #uuid "7ee10c12-4af0-5db5-b53d-68778b815ab0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{32}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96aa0f31-717f-5964-8ba0-b359e5264a03" :answer/id #uuid "96aa0f31-717f-5964-8ba0-b359e5264a03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351370 :question/worked-solution "Notice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- We already know the intersection of the curve with the line $y=0.$\nSo, the $x$-limits are \n$0\\le x\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/db/db0dd47348fb2f9a97c9e0514f74adae05830de7e03f1aea2886eaa95701200e.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region: \n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1-{x}^{2}\\}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\,dA={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}{x}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}{x}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[y]_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(1-{x}^{2}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}-{x}^{4})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}-{x}^{4})\\,dx & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{5}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351296 :question/worked-solution "Let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](images/aa/aa635ca5ef3198fea56d684b034de476a72e4ace2a4c51b37c6c59977036eb76.png)\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- The line $y=e$ intercepts the curve $y={e}^{x}$ at $x=1.$\nSo, the $x$-limits are \n$1\\le x\\le e.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/b7/b78021a06c9fea100b75c66a619c425345cda3666d84da018895be15a53af06d.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region: \n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,e\\le y\\le {e}^{x}\\}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dA={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}[{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)]}_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{x})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}dx & ={[\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{2}]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡e}{2}-\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186380978 :question/problem "Calculate ${∬}_{D}x\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le x\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over the type I region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le x\\}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{x}x\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{x}x\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{x}x\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[x{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{x}dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x{[\\,y\\,]}_{{x}^{3}}^{x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(x-{x}^{3})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}-{x}^{4})dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}-{x}^{4})dx & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186323953 :question/worked-solution "Let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](images/95/95ebd0a4eb874972b459e53eecf1d57650f63284698fcad967c09620ac01cd99.png)\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- The line $y=1-x$ intercepts the $x$-axis at $x=1.$\nSo, the $x$-limits are \n$0\\le x\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/d0/d048f20f2299722cee598cc1005237627ecdd7643e996b269f26b5a096f01f2f.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region: \n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x\\}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{(1+x+y)^{2}}\\,dA={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}\\frac{1}{(1+x+y)^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}\\frac{1}{(1+x+y)^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{-x+1}\\frac{1}{(1+x+y)^{2}}\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-\\frac{1}{1+x+y}]}_{0}^{-x+1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{1}{1+x+(1-x)}-(-\\frac{1}{1+x+0}))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{1+x})dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{1+x})dx & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-(0+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134020 :activity/expected-seconds 1080.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
